  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private Individual Digital Donations for NO NATION FASHION &#x2013; Support Migrants in BiH and Globally Thrive through Fashion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2017, mixed migration flows have increased significantly in the Western Balkan (WB) region, with over 192,000 irregular arrivals in 2022 recorded by the authorities. In response, IOM has been providing shelter, hygiene, protection, and a host of other assistance to migrants, as well as social cohesion initiatives with host communities. In December 2021, IOM BiH launched the No Nation Fashion (NNF) brand to promote sustainable development and social inclusion in communities hosting migrants. Building on this success, the present project proposes to support the expansion and growth of NNF to promote inclusion of migrants and local communities through fashion design and production. 
 
To do so, this project will enable private individuals to donate funds to the NNF Brand, which will in turn be used for the following: 
1. Maintain NNF workshops in reception facilities to build skills of interested migrants, such as design, sewing, tailoring, and modelling, in a safe and inclusive environment. 
2. To provide seed funding for materials and machines needed for migrants to create unique garments that showcase their skills 
3. Promote social and cultural joint activities and exchanges between host and migrant communities to celebrate diversity and build stronger inter-community bonds.</narrative>
  </description>
